# Livestock uses most farmland. How much of our food does it give?
subtitle: "Guess how much farmland goes to livestock, then how much of the world's food it gives back: four fifths of the land, under a fifth of the calories."
tags: ["food","earth","data"]
format: quiz
thumb: "band \"Most farmland feeds animals. And us?\" note \"?\""

## Livestock uses most farmland. How much of our food does it give?
affirm: playful
use: pie_chart
with:
    labels:
      - ' '
      - ' '
    values:
      - [80, 20]
      - [17, 83]
    stage: 0
    percent: false
sources:
    - id: owid
      title: Half of the world's habitable land is used for agriculture
      authors: Hannah Ritchie and Max Roser (Our World in Data)
      year: 2019
      url: https://ourworldindata.org/global-land-for-agriculture
      finding: livestock (grazing land plus cropland for feed) accounts for 80% of agricultural land; crops for humans 16%; meat, dairy and farmed fish provide 17% of the world's calories and 38% of its protein
    - id: fao
      title: FAOSTAT food balances and land use; Poore & Nemecek (2018), Science
      authors: UN Food and Agriculture Organization; J. Poore and T. Nemecek
      year: 2018
      finding: the land and food data behind Our World in Data's breakdown
    - id: kcal
      title: Land use per 1000 kilocalories (chart)
      authors: Our World in Data, from Poore & Nemecek (2018), Science
      year: 2018
      url: https://ourworldindata.org/grapher/land-use-kcal-poore
      finding: 'square metres per 1,000 kcal: beef (beef herd) 119, lamb & mutton 117, wheat & rye 1.4, rice 0.8, maize 0.7'

    icon cow size 280 set twemoji x 300 y 430 icon_look picture of "cow face" hidden true
    icon wheat size 280 set twemoji x 700 y 430 icon_look picture of "sheaf of rice" hidden true
    text t_land "LAND" #8f887c x 110 y 600 font_size 56 hidden true
    text t_food "FOOD" #8f887c x 110 y 600 font_size 56 hidden true
    text n80 "80% animals" #3d3833 cites ["owid"] x 540 y 300 font_size 60 hidden true
    text n17 "17%" #3d3833 cites ["owid"] x 580 y 525 font_size 64 hidden true
    text n83 "83% crops" #3d3833 cites ["owid"] x 430 y 280 font_size 60 hidden true
    text prot "protein: 38%" #b5482e cites ["owid"] x 880 y 470 font_size 38 hidden true
    shape sq_beef #b5482e shape rect x 360 y 420 width 380 height 380 style.fill #f3d9d3 hidden true
    shape sq_wheat #2f6b8f shape rect x 790 y 300 width 42 height 42 style.fill #cfe3ee hidden true
    icon i_beef size 150 set twemoji x 360 y 460 icon_look picture of "cow face" hidden true
    text l_beef "beef: 119 m²" #b5482e cites ["kcal"] x 360 y 330 font_size 48 hidden true
    icon i_wheat size 130 set twemoji x 790 y 410 icon_look picture of "sheaf of rice" hidden true
    text l_wheat "wheat: 1.4 m²" #2f6b8f cites ["kcal"] x 790 y 520 font_size 48 hidden true
    text l_per "land per 1,000 kcal" #8f887c x 790 y 610 font_size 40 hidden true
    text diet "what we eat" #2f6b8f x 875 y 330 font_size 40 hidden true
    text n17l "animals" #b5482e x 870 y 620 font_size 48 hidden true
    text n20l "crops" #2f6b8f x 200 y 500 font_size 48 hidden true

    card title "Livestock land: how much food?"

Farms grow food for us, and food for our animals. Which gets more land, and what does each give back?
    draw cow wheat

    erase cow wheat

    draw t_land

    ask "First, the land. Drag the edge: how much of all farmland goes to livestock?" on slice_1 store g default "50"
        right: Yes. The animals get most of it.
        wrong: See how much of the pie the animals really take.

Grazing land, plus the fields that grow animal feed: four fifths of all the farmland on Earth.
    draw n80 n20l

    erase t_land n80 n20l

So the animals must feed us well. Now let the same pie show the world's calories.
    draw t_food

    ask "Now drag the edge to where you think the animals' share of our calories goes." on slice_1 predict true store c default "50"
        right: Close. A small return on all that land.
        wrong: Much less than that: only about seventeen percent.

    animate stage 1 duration 2.5

Eighty percent of the land, for seventeen percent of the calories.
    draw n17 n17l

    hide slice_1 slice_2 n17 t_food n17l

Why? A cow burns most of what it eats just living. So a thousand calories of beef need about a hundred and twenty square metres of land.
    draw sq_beef i_beef l_beef

The same calories of wheat: under one and a half. About eighty times less.
    draw sq_wheat i_wheat l_wheat l_per

    erase sq_beef i_beef l_beef sq_wheat i_wheat l_wheat l_per

    show slice_1 slice_2 n17 t_food n17l

Turn it round: the other fifth of farmland, crops, gives us eighty-three percent of our calories.
    draw n83

Animal foods do better on protein, about thirty-eight percent of it, so that land is not simply wasted.
    draw prot

Still, how much land farming needs depends less on how we farm than on what we eat.
    draw diet

